Hi Patrio Gabriel,

Three features worth trying once your first requests are landing. Each one =
is a single parameter change. Each one earns its place in production code a=
nd none of them require a new integration or a different endpoint.

See the feature docs ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/quickstart?utm_source=3De=
mail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=3Da13_=
close&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA9+Featu=
re+Trio&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )

=E2=80=83

Streaming ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/streaming?utm_source=
=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=3D=
a13_close&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA9+F=
eature+Trio&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io ). Set strea=
m=3DTrue and tokens arrive as they generate. Same endpoint, same auth, one =
parameter. Perceived latency drops from seconds to the first token, which i=
s the difference between a chat UI that feels alive and one that feels brok=
en. Agents that stream partial results to a frontend get a noticeable UX li=
ft for zero code cost.

Structured outputs ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/features/structured-outputs=
?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm=
_content=3Da13_close&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_con=
tent=3DA9+Feature+Trio&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )=
=2E Pass a JSON schema via response_for=
mat and OpenRouter enforces it at the=20=
API level. No regex parsing, no retry loops when the model returns malforme=
d JSON, no "please respond in valid JSON" prompt engineering. Works on ever=
y model that supports the format, and the router respects it when you use o=
penrouter/auto.

Provider preferences ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/features/provider-routing=
?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm=
_content=3Da13_close&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_con=
tent=3DA9+Feature+Trio&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )=
=2E Pin specific providers, exclude oth=
ers, set latency floors and throughput=
 minimums. When a model has multiple providers behind it, you decide which =
backend serves each request. Set {"sort": "price"} to always pick the cheap=
est, or an allowlist to lock routing to providers you trust.

=E2=80=83

ALL THREE AT ONCE

